{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgmgpf4bJRtLxPCWxsJTx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**What I decided:** Psagot Trade looks OK, not a scam, so I'd probably open the account, but I'm only fairly sure. What decided it was the \"דמי חשבון קבועים 0.00 ₪ לחודש\", so there's no monthly fee just for having the account.\n\n**What it charges, as far as I got it:**\n- Buying or selling: \"0.07%\" with \"מינימום לפעולה 2.00 ₪\". So each trade costs at least 2 shekels.\n- Something called \"דמי ניהול פיקדון ניירות ערך\": \"0.03% לרבעון\". I think that's a fee for holding my stuff, but I'm not sure.\n- Changing shekels to dollars: I saw \"1.5 אגורות לדולר\" and then \"0.5%\" further down, both labelled \"המרת מטבע\". I don't know which one is real.\n- You need \"מינימום לפתיחת חשבון: 10,000 ₪\". I have 30k, so that's fine.\n\n**What I can buy:** It says \"אפשר\" next to \"קרן סל\" and \"יחידות של קרן נאמנות\". So the S&P thing my friends talk about should be possible. \"ניירות ערך זרים\" says \"לא ידוע\" in orange, which kind of worried me. I didn't read the long text under it.\n\n**What bothered me most:** There's a section \"מה כתוב בפרסום, ומה במסמכים\" where some rows say \"המסמך אומר אחרת\":\n- Their ad says \"ללא עמלת המרה\", but the document says 1.5 agorot per dollar.\n- The ad says \"פטור מעמלת ק/מ\" on funds, but the document says 0.07% with a 2 ₪ minimum.\n\nSo their ads lie a bit. I'd trust the document numbers, and those are still small.\n\n**How I went through it:**\n1. The big heading \"פסגות ניירות ערך (פסגות טרייד)\". It was the right page, and I know Psagot from ads.\n2. The fee boxes under \"העמלות\".\n3. \"מה אפשר לקנות כאן\".\n4. The ad-vs-document comparison.\n5. The minimum to open an account.\n6. The two buttons at the bottom.\n\n**What I skipped:**\n- The search box on the left.\n- The \"דמי משמרת\" row. I don't know that word, and it scrolled past between screens.\n- The fold 